1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,604
Capacities are sums of volumes.

2
00:00:02,604 --> 00:00:11,393
The vital capacity, the most you can breathe out after the deepest breath, is tidal plus both reserves: four thousand six hundred.

3
00:00:11,393 --> 00:00:17,083
Add the residual volume for the total lung capacity: five thousand eight hundred.

4
00:00:17,083 --> 00:00:24,231
One trap: a spirometer can never see the residual volume, so it cannot measure total lung capacity either.

